    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Serengeti covers about 14,750 square kilometres of grassland and acacia woodland in northern Tanzania. It runs north to the Kenyan border, where it meets the Masai Mara, and borders the Ngorongoro Conservation Area to the southeast.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The name comes from the Maasai word for endless plains. The national park was set up in 1951 and became a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1981. Granite kopjes break the flat horizon and give big cats a place to watch from.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "June to October is dry, with river crossings in the north from about July, while January and February bring the calving in the south. Pack neutral colours, as tsetse flies are drawn to dark blue and black.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
